module gunbc.guarantee_stall.floor_cost_basis_boundedness_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { OutsideTheLadder, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, AwaitsOneGrounding, UncountedNotEnumerable, climbs_when }

// NO MEASUREMENT CAMPAIGN CAN DISCHARGE THIS ARM, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS A STALL RATHER THAN UNBUILT
// WORK. `gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable` states that its restoration
// trigger's conjunct (ii) requires the cost basis to be INVARIANT OR BOUNDED BY CONSTRUCTION. The
// invariance arm is measured and REFUTED. This row is about the other arm, at its own subject grain
// -- not the whole disjunction, because collapsing the two is the exact defect gunbc#10260 repaired
// in that row's own text, and repeating it here would reintroduce it one file away.
//
// THE REACHABILITY RESULT, which is what makes the blocker AwaitsOneGrounding rather than
// ClimbableButUnbuilt. For observed pairwise ratios r1..rn with M = max(r1..rn), the evidence
// establishes only that every bound K valid for those observations satisfies K >= M. Adding samples
// may leave M unchanged or RAISE it; it cannot establish `for every admitted execution pair, ratio
// <= K`. So an observed maximum is a FLOOR on any valid bound, never a bound -- and a percentile, a
// confidence interval, or a long run of non-exceedances is not a substitute for a construction-
// derived one. The rung_drop row already says this of one measurement; what is recorded here is the
// general statement, so a future lane does not read that sentence as an invitation to sample more
// hosts. A 12-run campaign reporting a worst-observed 2.280x is exactly the artifact that would be
// offered, and it does not touch the arm.
//
// WHY THE PREREQUISITE IS A GROUNDING AND NOT AN IMPLEMENTATION: there is no closed admitted
// envelope with every basis-varying component accounted for, so the work is not a decided
// construction merely unstarted -- it is unspecifiable until that authority exists. The four
// conjuncts below are ONE conjunctive grounding, not four alternative routes, and the trigger says
// so, because a trigger satisfiable by any one of them would retire this row with the capability
// still dead -- the section 4b(3) grain mismatch, arriving here as a section 4b(2) trigger.
//
// CEILING IS GUARANTEED AND NOT IMPOSSIBLE: a bound derived from admitted components and caps is a
// proof from modeled structure, but an execution that exceeds it stays authorable. What the climb
// removes is the silent acceptance, not the ability to write the program.
//
// CURRENT IS OutsideTheLadder, AND THE READING THAT MADE IT `Mitigatable` WAS RUNG INFLATION ACROSS A
// SUBJECT BOUNDARY. This row first cited the drop row's `acceptance still fail-closed` clause as
// though it spoke for THIS arm. It does not: that clause is about attempt safety and verdict
// availability, which are a neighbouring path. Read the deciding consumer instead of the prose --
// `v2.workflow.required_floor.claim_safety_outcome` takes seven parameters, none of which is or
// derives from any construction-bound authority, and branches only on `reached_verdict`, then
// `observed_cpu_ms` against `cpu_limit_ms`, then `observed_wall_ms` against `wall_limit_ms`. So the
// absence of the boundedness arm accompanies `CompletedWithinSafetyLimits` and
// `CompletedPastSafetyLimit` ALIKE, and no output of that function varies with it. A refusal there is
// evidence that one execution crossed an attempt-safety limit, never that the arm is missing.
//
// Nothing observes this arm and nothing blocks on it, so no harm is contained at its own grain and
// rung one is not occupied. Section 4b makes a class's current rung the MINIMUM over its in-scope
// paths, so the fail-closed neighbour cannot raise this silent one. The same standard is already
// applied one module away: `v2.workflow.required_floor`'s PREEMPTION-1 drop rules that for an
// `OpaqueHostCallUnbounded` claim the two limits `are not even mitigatable -- they observe nothing
// and block nothing at the moment the cost accrues`. This row now holds itself to the rule its
// neighbour states rather than to a sentence quoted from a different subject.
//
// AND WHY THIS IS A STALL RATHER THAN A SECOND DROP, which the drop row settles in its own words:
// `PREVIOUS RUNG: none for environment-independent claim-cost qualification -- that guarantee was
// never held, and saying it was would be inventing a rung to drop from.` Nothing was lost, so a
// drop's previous/temporary/reason fields have no answer here. The two rows are also different
// facts: the drop states the standing unavailability, this states that one named restoration
// conjunct is unreachable BY MEASUREMENT and what would reach it.
// THE CONVERSION BELOW IS A CARRIER REPAIR, NOT A CORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S CONTENT. Read this
// before drawing a conclusion about this row's author from the diff that added `climbs_when`.
//
// THE ORDER, MEASURED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS BECAUSE AN EARLIER DRAFT OF THIS COMMENT HAD IT
// BACKWARDS. The carrier landed FIRST: 86be37f355 (gunbc#10582) at 17:21:02 already declared
// `next_rung_trigger: NextRungTrigger` and supplied `climbs_when`. This row landed at 18:35:47,
// SEVENTY-FOUR MINUTES LATER, in 45074b4e9c (gunbc#10281), spelling the field as a bare `String`.
// `git merge-base --is-ancestor` answers YES in the carrier-before-row direction and NO in the
// other. So this is NOT a migration that forgot a caller, and gunbc#10582 stranded nothing: AN
// OLD-FORMAT DECLARATION LANDED ONTO A CARRIER THAT HAD ALREADY CHANGED.
//
// THE MEASURED CONSEQUENCE. 31 of the 33 rows in this directory use the constructor; this one did
// not, and the closure enumerating them refuses with `type mismatch: expected
// 'Product(NextRungTrigger)', got 'Primitive(String)'`. A branch merging main could not resolve
// that closure until this conversion was made.
//
// THE MECHANISM, IN ONE LINE: DISCOVERING AN IDENTITY SO IT CAN RECEIVE A DISPOSITION IS NOT THE
// SAME OPERATION AS PREPARING AND EXECUTING ITS DEPENDENCY CLOSURE. The witness DEPENDS ON the
// roster -- live folds reaching the trigger, not a dead import. The required run ADMITS that
// witness module into PREPARATION -- it does not. The first does not establish the second.
//
// THE INCIDENT, READ FROM THE ARTIFACT RATHER THAN INFERRED. The required-floor-disposition TSV
// (artifact 9975676354, run 33986383584 at 2f8819b891, checked against its published SHA-256)
// carries all ELEVEN identities of `test.claim.guarantee_stall_witness_test` as
// `disposition = declined_outside_gate_closure`, `outcome = not_executed` -- including
// `every_live_stall_names_a_next_rung_trigger` and `every_live_stall_trigger_is_admitted`.
//
// SO THE FLOOR DID NOT LIE, AND SAYING IT DID WOULD BE BOTH WRONG AND WEAKER. Every per-identity
// disposition is exactly right: the run reported, honestly and per identity, that these witnesses
// DID NOT RUN. What is wrong is that an AGGREGATE reported SUCCESS over a population that had
// already excluded them. A defender can rebut "the floor lied about eleven witnesses"; nobody can
// rebut "the floor said not_executed and the aggregate said success".
//
// THAT IS DENOMINATOR LOSS -- an aggregate verdict computed over an already-narrowed population,
// so success never establishes that the ADMITTED set survived. The same shape is carried as an
// open P0 finding at the install boundary; two boundaries exhibiting one shape is the fact worth
// recording, not two incidents. The narrowing itself is
// `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.preparation_membership_derived_from_the_execution_selector`, which
// is the authority for it; this comment mints no second wording.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT LICENSE, stated so nobody reaches for it: it is not an argument for compiling
// everything whenever the selector is uncertain. That is the absorbing fallback -- denominated in
// the corpus rather than the change, growing until the budget breaks instead of the build. A
// widening must be explicit, bounded, and credited only for the population it actually restores.
//
// TWO EXPLANATIONS WERE OFFERED FOR THE GREEN AND BOTH ARE WITHDRAWN, recorded because an
// unmeasured mechanism in a permanent comment is worse than no mechanism. The first was that the
// migration missed a caller -- refuted by the ordering above. The second was that the roster is
// enumerated somewhere the required floor does not compile -- refuted by the witnesses existing,
// consuming it through live folds, and being reported per identity. What is measured is that they
// were DISCOVERED and DECLINED, never prepared.
//
// THE QUESTION THIS OPENS is sharper than either withdrawn explanation, and no census at the
// carrier's own PR could have answered it: DOES ADMISSION VALIDATE AN INCOMING DECLARATION AGAINST
// THE CARRIER CURRENT AT PLACEMENT? A clean merge and an active author do not establish
// compatibility with an intervening authority change. The discriminating evidence for that work is
// an incoming old-format constructor under the new carrier, REFUSED BY AN EXECUTING REQUIRED
// CONSUMER, with the valid `climbs_when` construction still accepted; a roster-membership check
// establishes neither half.
//
// THE CONVERSION IS MECHANICAL AND VERIFIED AS SUCH: the capability text is byte-identical at 321
// characters, and `awaiting: []` discards nothing -- the original trigger carried no referent
// provenance to lose. It restores resolution; IT CLOSES NOTHING about admission.

data floor_cost_basis_boundedness_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "the BOUNDEDNESS-BY-CONSTRUCTION arm of conjunct (ii) of gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable's restoration trigger: repeated execution measurement cannot establish it, because every observed maximum is a LOWER bound on the smallest valid bound rather than an upper bound over the admitted envelope",
  current: OutsideTheLadder,
  ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
  blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding {
    grounding: "a typed construction-bound authority for the declared basis and subject grain, consumed by the required-floor verdict at that same grain, which (1) closes the admitted execution envelope; (2) accounts for every component capable of changing the basis, by removing it from the measured subject, charging it to that subject, assigning it an enforced finite cap, or refusing the envelope; (3) derives a finite bound from those admitted components and caps rather than from an observed sample maximum; and (4) carries discriminating execution evidence over the admitted corner cases plus an over-bound control refused on the real acceptance path"
  },
  population: UncountedNotEnumerable {
    reason: "the subject is ONE ARM of conjunct (ii) of a restoration trigger authored as prose inside gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable. The population this carrier reports is the EXPOSURE, not a roster of the source artifacts that carry or discuss the subject, and the exposed set here is every required identity for which the CPU deadline is armed, derived per run. That set is produced by execution rather than declared in source, so no authored list in this standing row would be true when written. It is finite, not mathematically infinite, and a run may well emit its own occurrence roster; what does not exist is a stable source-level authority this row could name. TWO EARLIER REVISIONS OF THIS FIELD WERE WRONG IN DIFFERENT WAYS, recorded because the second failure is the instructive one. The first list named gunbc.floor_cost_distribution.RunCost.eval_steps, a field that does not exist -- RunCost declares run and rows -- so its BoundedPopulation was not an identity join and the bound was never real. The second revision substituted a symbol that does exist, v2.workflow.required_floor.claim_safety_outcome, and was still wrong, because the defect was the SHAPE rather than the bad member: the list enumerated CARRIERS -- an instrument column, a deciding consumer, and the parent drop -- which is one-carrier-answers-for-the-whole-population, the move `gunbc.guarantee_stall.two_nat_authorities_stall` rejects under this same StallPopulation carrier even though its own declaration half and four direct importers are perfectly enumerable. THE FUTURE BOUNDARY IS NOT A TYPED SPLIT OF THE PARENT TRIGGER. Giving the arm a typed source identity would make the SUBJECT referable and may be worth doing on its own, but it neither enumerates the exposed required identities nor is needed to; naming that new arm identity here would repeat the same rejected move one level down. What would permit an honest BoundedPopulation is a typed PRODUCER of the exposed population at this grain -- a derivation joining a run's required-identity dispositions to the CpuDeadlineArmed policy, or another closed authority that enumerates every affected identity",
  },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "the construction-bound authority named in this row's grounding EXISTS and is CONSUMED by the required-floor verdict at the declared subject grain, with its over-bound control refused on the real acceptance path; no volume of execution sampling retires this row, and a widening of the measurement campaign does not move it"),
}
